Subject: R2, CBOR nesting limit, duplicate and numeric text map keys
Reason: Attacker-controlled authData is CBOR-decoded before the signature check, and about 100 KB of nested arrays segfaulted PHP 8.5 (audit 3); arrays, maps and tags now nest at most 16 deep, and a map key that repeats or that PHP would coerce to an integer (text "3") is rejected, as CTAP2 canonical CBOR (L3 6.5.1) has neither.

diff -ruN a/CBOR/CborDecoder.php b/CBOR/CborDecoder.php
--- a/CBOR/CborDecoder.php
+++ b/CBOR/CborDecoder.php
@@ -22,6 +22,9 @@
     const CBOR_MAJOR_MAP = 5;
     const CBOR_MAJOR_BYTE_STRING = 2;
 
+    // Deepest nesting of arrays, maps and tags; WebAuthn structures nest 3 deep.
+    const MAX_DEPTH = 16;
+
     /**
      * @param ByteBuffer|string $bufOrBin
      * @return mixed
@@ -60,9 +63,14 @@
